  "macroTheme": "Moody's strips US of last Aaa rating (downgrades to Aa1) as April CPI +3.8% YoY cements Fed hold. NAS100 hit year high 29,678 on Trump-Xi Beijing summit before Friday reversal. Silver crashed 14% from 88.88 peak. NVDA earnings Thu May 22 is the pivotal forward catalyst.",
  "macroOverview": "Week of May 11-17 defined by two competing forces: risk-on optimism from Trump's Beijing summit with Xi Jinping driving NAS100 to year high 29,678 and Dow above 50,000 (May 14), versus inflation shock from April CPI +3.8% YoY (highest since May 2023). By Friday May 15 the inflation side won: US 10-year yield jumped to 4.544% (highest in nearly a year), silver fell 7% on the day, and gold sold off from its 4,765 peak. Late Friday Moody's downgraded US sovereign debt from Aaa to Aa1, citing ballooning deficits. The downgrade is the dominant Monday open story: dollar under pressure, gold supported, equities facing another leg of selling. NVDA Q1 earnings Thursday May 22 remains the most pivotal equity catalyst for the period.",
